hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"667","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am warning you about Hell, I am warning you about Hell, I am warning you about"
"668","“We stopped with Abu Hashim bin ‘Utbah, who had been stabbed, and Mu’awiyah came to visit him. Abu Hashim wept and Mu’awiyah said to him: ‘Why are you weeping, O maternal uncle? Is there some pain bothering you, or is it because of this world, the best of which has already passed?’ He said: ‘It is not for any of these reasons. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me some advice and I wish that I had followed it. He ﷺ said: “There may come a time when you will see wealth divided among the people, and all you will need of that is a servant and a mount to ride in the cause of Allah.” That time came, but I accumulated wealth.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4103)"
"669","""When Allah loves a slave, He prevents him from the world, just as one of you prevents his sick from water."" Another chain reports a similar narration. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2036)"
"670","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""Whoever accepts Islam, and his sustenance is sufficient for him, and he remains patient over it, then he has succeeded."
"671","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever among you wakes up physically healthy, feeling safe and secure within himself, with food for the day, it is as if he acquired the whole world.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4141)"
"672","I had a curtain on which there were pictures, and I hung it on the door. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saw it, he said: ""Take it down, for it reminds me of the world."
"673","There should be a bedding for a man. a bedding for his wife and the third one for the guest, and the fourth one is for the Satan. (Using translation from Muslim 2084)"
"674","The son of Adam does not fill any vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the son of Adam to eat a few morsels that keep his back straight. If he must (eat more), then he should fill one third (of his stomach) with food, one third with drink, and one third with air (for breathing).”"
"675","I stood at the door of Paradise and I found that the overwhelming majority of those who entered therein was that of poor persons and the wealthy persons were detained to get into that. The denizens of Hell were commanded to get into Hell, and I stood upon the door of Fire and the majority amongst them who entered there was that of women. (Using translation from Muslim 2736)"
"676","“The poor believers will enter Paradise half a day – five hundred years – before the rich.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4122)"
"677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying: ""Give glad tidings to the poor emigrants that they will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy people."
"678","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saying: ""Indeed, the poor emigrants will enter Paradise seventy years (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these words are:) forty years before the wealthy people on the Day of Resurrection."
"679","“Richness is not an abundance of worldly goods, rather richness is contentment with one’s lot.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4137)"
"680","I thought that he must have gone to him for some important matter that Marwan wanted to ask him about. I asked Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: He asked us about some things which we had heard from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). (Sayyiduna Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him, said) I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “May Allah make happy the one who hears a hadith from us and then conveys it to another, for sometimes the one who receives knowledge conveys it to someone more knowledgeable than himself, and sometimes the one who receives knowledge is not actually a scholar. There are three things about which a Muslim’s heart does not deceive: making deeds sincere for Allah, wishing well for the Muslim rulers, and sticking to their community, for their supplication encompasses those who are absent. Whoever’s intention is for the world, Allah will scatter his affairs and place poverty before his eyes, and he will get nothing from the world except what is written for him. And whoever’s intention is for the Hereafter, Allah will gather his affairs, place contentment in his heart, and the world will come to him humbled.”"
"681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Now observe and tell me, who among those before you is the person of the lowest status?"" I observed, and there was a poor man sitting in old clothes. I said: ""This person."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This (poor person), on the Day of Resurrection, will be better in the sight of Allah Almighty than (rich men like) a whole earth full of such people."
"682","I saw seventy companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the Suffah. None of them had a cloak; they only had a small lower garment or a single sheet which they would wrap around themselves as a mantle and tie it behind their backs."
"683","narrates: In the blessed era of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, our food consisted of only two black things: dates and water."
"684","narrates: Whoever tells you that we used to eat our fill of dates, he has not spoken the truth to you. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) conquered Qurayza, we received some dates and fat."
"685","I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then, do you think that having little wealth is poverty? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: True prosperity is the prosperity of the heart, and true poverty is the poverty of the heart. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked me about a man from the Quraysh. He said: Do you know so-and-so? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What is your opinion about him and how is he regarded? I said: When he asks for something, it is given to him; when he comes somewhere, he is allowed to enter. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked me about a man from the people of Suffah and said: Do you know so-and-so? I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah! I do not know him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to mention his lineage to me until I recognized him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah! Now I have recognized him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What is your opinion about him and how is he regarded? I said: He is a poor man from the people of Suffah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He (the poor man) is better than the earth full of people like the other (rich man). I said: O Messenger of Allah! That person was not given any share of what was given to the other. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If he has been given goodness, then he is more deserving of it, and if it has been withheld from him, then goodness has been granted to him."
"686","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever the sun rises, there are two angels on its sides who make this announcement: 'O Allah! Grant more in return to the one who spends (in Your way), and cause loss to the one who does not spend.'"
"687","“This world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4113)"
"688","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."
"689","The Prophet said concerning the Verse: ""Every day He is (engaged) in some affair."" ""His affairs include forgiving sins, relieving distress, raising some people and bringing others low."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 202)"
"690","“I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘There is nothing left of this world except trials and tribulations.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4035)"
"691","narrates: One night the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah, the Exalted, is free from every defect. How many tribulations have been sent down and how many doors of treasures have been opened. Wake up the women who are in the chamber, for many women who are veiled in this world will be unveiled on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"692","I stood at the door of Paradise and I found that the overwhelming majority of those who entered therein was that of poor persons and the wealthy persons were detained to get into that. The denizens of Hell were commanded to get into Hell, and I stood upon the door of Fire and the majority amongst them who entered there was that of women. (Using translation from Muslim 2736)"
"693","I would reply, “Yes!” When I said, “Now I do not hear it,” he returned to the path. Then he said, “I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) doing the same.”"
"694","The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Beware! Indeed, the dirham and the dinar destroyed the people before you, and they will also destroy you."
"695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took a handful of dates and sent them to one of his noble wives. Then he took a handful of dates and sent them to his wives. Then he sent them again, and he desired this, and he did this several times, and he desired this."
"696","I saw that she had done something new there. Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) informed Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) about this, so she took down the curtain and removed the mat, put the things that were on it aside, and wore old clothes herself. Then Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) presented himself before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then came to her. He embraced her (Lady Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her) and said: ""Remain like this, may my parents be sacrificed for you."
"698","ʿAbdullah bin ʿUmar said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of my shoulder and said, 'Be in this world as if you were a stranger or a traveler."" The sub-narrator added: Ibn ʿUmar used to say, ""If you survive till the evening, do not expect to be alive in the morning, and if you survive till the morning, do not expect to be alive in the evening, and take from your health for your sickness, and (take) from your life for your death."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6416)"
"699","It was narrated from Ibn Buraidah that his father said: ""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The nobility of the people of this world, that which they (always) go to, is wealth.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3225)"
"700","It was narrated from Ibn Buraidah that his father said: ""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The nobility of the people of this world, that which they (always) go to, is wealth.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3225)"
"701","I came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ as he was reciting:"" Abundance diverts you"" (cii. 1). He said: The son of Adam claims: My wealth, my wealth. And he (the Holy Prophet) said: O son of Adam. is there anything as your belonging except that which you consumed, which you utilised, or which you wore and then it was worn out or you gave as charity and sent it forward? (Using translation from Muslim 2958a)"
"702","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the world can be given through what the son of Adam eats; whatever comes out of the body of the son of Adam. Even though he puts spices and salt in it, you should consider what it becomes (after staying in a person's stomach)."
"703","narrates: No one could surpass the she-camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Al-Adhba’, whenever there was a race with her, she would always win. Once, a Bedouin came riding a camel and raced with her, and he surpassed her. This was hard on the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) noticed this on their faces, he said: ""It is incumbent upon Allah that whenever He elevates something in this world, He also brings it down."
"704","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was lying on it. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw both of them, he sat up straight. Both of them saw that there were marks of the bed on the side of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep. They said: O Messenger of Allah! The bed and bedding that we see you using, does its hardness not cause you discomfort, while Caesar and Chosroes rest on silk and brocade? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Do not say this, for the beds of Caesar and Chosroes will be in Hell, and my bed and my bedding, their place is in Paradise."
"705","""Glad tidings to whoever is guided to Islam, his livelihood was sufficient and he was satisfied."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2349)"
"706","The people asked: O Abu Abdullah! Why are you anxious? While you have the honor of being foremost in goodness. You participated in battles alongside the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and took part in great victories. Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi replied: This thing is making me anxious, that when our beloved Prophet (peace be upon him) departed from us, he took a covenant from us. He said: ""It is sufficient for any one of you for a day to have only as much as a rider's provision for travel."" So this is what is making me anxious. Then, when the wealth of Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) was gathered, its value was fifteen dinars. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Aamir is Aamir bin Abd Qais, and Salman al-Khair refers to Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"707","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We were present in a cave with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when this Surah was revealed to him. So I learned this Surah from his own recitation, even though it had just been revealed to him a short while ago. I do not know at which verse he ended it—was it at «فباي حديث بعده يومنون» or at this verse «واذا قبل لهم اركعو الا يركعون »? In the meantime, a snake appeared and then entered its hole, so the Prophet (peace and"
"708","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) in a cave. Surah Mursalat was revealed to him. He recited it and I learned it from his tongue; it had been revealed to him just a short while before. Meanwhile, a snake appeared before us. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Kill it! We quickly rushed towards it, but it went away. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It has"
"709","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whoever loves the world, this thing harms his Hereafter; whoever loves the Hereafter, then this thing harms his world. So give preference to that which is everlasting over that which will perish."
"710","""Do not take to the estate, such that you become desirous of the world."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2328)"
"711","When one of you looks at one who stands at a higher level than you in regard to wealth and physical structure he should also see one who stands at a lower level than you in regard to these things (in which he stands) at a higher level (as compared to him). (Using translation from Muslim 2963a)"
"712","When one of you looks at one who stands at a higher level than you in regard to wealth and physical structure he should also see one who stands at a lower level than you in regard to these things (in which he stands) at a higher level (as compared to him). (Using translation from Muslim 2963a)"
"713","“Look at those who are beneath you and do not look at those who are above you, for it is more suitable that you should not consider as less the blessing of Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4142)"
"714","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person looks at someone above him in wealth and lineage, he should also look at someone below him in wealth and lineage."
"715","I replied: It is with me. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Give it in charity. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Due to being busy, I could not do this. Then he asked: O Aisha! What did you do with that gold? I replied: It is with me. He said: Bring it to me. Lady Aisha says: I brought it, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) took it in his pouch and said: ""What will be thought about Muhammad if he were to appear before Allah Almighty in such a state that this is with him? What will be thought about Muhammad (peace be upon him) if he were to appear before Allah Almighty in such a state that this is with him?"
"716","""Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2559)"
"717","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The strong one is not the one who overcomes others; the strong one is the one who controls himself at the time of anger."
"718","The Paradise is surrounded by hardships and the Hell-Fire is surrounded by temptations. (Using translation from Muslim 2822)"
"719","The Paradise is surrounded by hardships and the Hell-Fire is surrounded by temptations. (Using translation from Muslim 2822)"
"720","I bought the land from you, I did not buy the gold from you.' The man who had sold the land said: 'I sold you the land and everything in it.' The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Both of them appointed a third person as an arbitrator. The person who was appointed as the arbitrator asked: 'Do you have any children?' One of them said: 'I have a son.' The other said: 'I have a daughter.' The arbitrator said: 'Marry the boy to the girl, and spend (the wealth) on yourselves and also give charity.'"
"721","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: What is lawful is clear and what is unlawful is clear, but between them are certain doubtful things. I give you an example for this. Allah has a preserve, and Allah's preserve is the things He has declared unlawful. He who pastures (his animals) round the preserve will soon fall into it. He who falls into doubtful things will soon be courageous. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3329)"
"722","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also said: ""Goodness is tranquility and evil is doubt."" (Sayyiduna Imam Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, also said) Once some dates of charity were presented to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). I took one of those dates and put it in my mouth. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took that date, took its saliva, and put it back in the date. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah! There is no harm to you regarding the date this child took. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for us, the family of Muhammad. (Sayyiduna Imam Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, also said) I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicating: ""O Allah! Keep us steadfast on guidance among those whom You have guided! Grant us well-being among those whom You have granted well-being! Be our guardian among those whom You have taken as guardians! Bless for us what You have given us, and protect us from the evil of what You have decreed. Surely, You decree and none can decree against You. Whomever You take as a guardian cannot be disgraced. You are Blessed and Exalted."
"723","I need a she-camel on which we can ride and some goats whose milk my family can milk. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Have you people become so incapable that you cannot even be like the old women of Bani Israel? The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! What was the matter of the old women of Bani Israel? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: When Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) set out from Egypt with Bani Israel, they lost their way. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) asked: What is the reason for this? Their scholars informed him: When Sayyiduna Yusuf (peace be upon him) was near death, he took a firm covenant from us by Allah that when we leave Egypt, we will take his body with us. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) asked: Who knows the location of his grave? A person told him: An old woman from Bani Israel knows. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) called for that woman. She came to him. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) said: Guide me to the grave of Sayyiduna Yusuf (peace be upon him). The woman said: I will not do so until you give me my compensation. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) asked: What is your compensation? She replied: That I be with you in Paradise. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) did not like to say this to her, so Allah revealed to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) that give her what she is asking for. Then the woman took them to a place from where water was gushing forth. The woman said: Stop this water. They stopped the water. The woman said: Now open it. They opened it, and from there the bones of Sayyiduna Yusuf (peace be upon him) appeared. When they returned to that land, the path became as clear as daylight."
"724","I was also with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"725","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ar-Rahman's Hand is full, He spends without any decrease, night and day.' He said: 'Do you not see how much He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth, yet it has not decreased what is in His Hand, and His Throne is over the water, and in His Other Hand is the Mizan (Scale) which He raises and lowers.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3045)"
"726","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An entire nation entered Paradise because they did not cauterize, did not practice ruqyah (incantations), and relied upon their Lord."
"727","I went to Ubayy b. Ka’b and said him : I am confused about Divine decree, so tell me something by means of which Allah may remove the confusion from my mind. He replied : were Allah to punish everyone in the heavens and in the earth. He would do so without being unjust to them, and were he to show mercy to them his mercy would be much better than their actions merited. Were you to spend in support of Allah’s cause an amount of gold equivalent to Uhud, Allah would not accept it from you till you believed in divine decree and knew that what has come to you could not miss you and that what has missed you could not come to you. Were you to die believing anything else you would enter Hell. He said : I then went to ‘Abd Allah b. MAs’ud and he said something to the same effect. I next went to Hudhaifah b. al-Yaman and he said something to the same effect. I next went to Zaid b. Thabit who told me something from the Prophet (May peace be upon him) to the same effect. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4699)"
"728","I am amazed at the affair of the believer; indeed, whatever decision Allah Almighty makes regarding him, it is better for him."
"729","narrates: Sometimes three months would pass in the household of Muhammad (peace be upon him) during which they would not be able to light a fire. Their food would consist only of water and dates. There were some families of the Ansar around us who had goats in their gardens, so sometimes people from one of those families would send fresh milk from their goats to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would drink that milk."
"730","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: *“If you were to rely upon Allah with true reliance, Allah would provide for you as He provides for the birds: they go out in the morning hungry and return in the evening full.”*"
"731","The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""Tie it and then place your trust in Allah."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narrator named Ya'qub is Ya'qub bin Amr bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Umayyah Zumri. He belonged to the people of Hijaz. He is well-known and trustworthy."
"732","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Recite the Qur’an as long as your hearts are inclined towards it, and when your attention begins to wander, then get up (and leave its recitation).”"
"733","I passed by you while you were performing prayer and reciting in a low voice. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: I was making Him hear Whom I was supplicating to. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Umar! I also passed by you, and you were reciting in a loud voice. He replied: O Messenger of Allah! I wanted to wake up the sleeping person and hoped for reward through it. The narrator states: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): Raise your voice a little, and to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Lower your voice a little."
"734","The Prophet ﷺ said: One who recites the Qur'an in a loud voice is like one who gives alms openly; and one who recites the Qur'an quietly is one who gives alms secretly. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1333)"
"735","I said: Should I recite it to you while the Qur'an has been revealed to you? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I desire to hear it from someone else. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I began reciting Surah An-Nisa before him. When I reached this verse: ""Then how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness over all of them?"" I looked towards the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and his eyes were flowing with tears."
"736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Learn the recitation of the Qur’an from four people: Abdullah bin Mas’ud, Salim the freed slave of Abu Hudhaifah, Mu’adh bin Jabal, and Ubayy bin Ka’b.”"
"737","The Messenger of Allah taught me to recite it. Sayyiduna Ubayy says: I went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! You taught me to recite such and such verses. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes! That man said: You taught me to recite such and such verses. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes! Jibreel and Mikaeel came to me. Jibreel sat on my right side and Mikaeel sat on my left side. Jibreel said: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), recite the Qur'an according to one mode (harf). Mikaeel said: Ask for more. So I said: Tell me more ways. Then Jibreel said: Recite it according to two modes. Mikaeel said: Ask for more, until it reached seven modes. Then Jibreel said: Recite it up to seven modes. Each of them is sufficient and complete."
"738","I ask Allah Almighty for His pardon and His forgiveness (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) His help and His pardon. Then ask Allah for ease for these people, because they will not be able to bear it. Jibreel went back, then he returned and said: Indeed, Allah Almighty has commanded you to teach your Ummah the recitation of the Qur'an according to two modes. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I ask Allah Almighty for His pardon and His forgiveness (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) His help and His pardon. Then request ease for these people, because they will not be able to bear it. Jibreel went back, then he returned and said: Indeed, Allah Almighty has commanded you to teach your Ummah to recite this Qur'an in three modes. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I ask Allah Almighty for His pardon and His forgiveness (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) His help and His pardon. Then request ease for them, because they will not be able to bear it. Jibreel went back, then he returned and said: Indeed, Allah Almighty has commanded you that you may recite this Qur'an in seven modes. Whoever recites in any one of them, he will have recited correctly."
"739","I have been sent to an unlettered nation among whom are boys and girls, old women and old men."" So Jibreel said: ""Guide them that they may recite according to any one of the seven modes."
"740","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was sitting in the mosque when a man entered and began to recite (the Qur'an). His recitation seemed unfamiliar to me. Then another man came and he recited differently from his companion. Then he completed his prayer. Then both of them went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: O Messenger of Allah! This person has recited in a manner that seemed unfamiliar to me, then the other person reci"
"741","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon h"
"742","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an has been revealed on seven modes (ahruf)."
"743","The Qur'an was revealed upon seven letters."" (These words of the narration are:) The Wise, The Knowledgeable, The Forgiving, The Merciful. These are the words of Muhammad bin Amr, which have been included in the text of the narration. The original narration contains only the words up to ""seven letters."
"744","I know more about Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) than all of you, for I could write whatever I wished."" Then he died. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was informed of this, he said: ""The earth will not accept him."" The narrator states: Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) related this incident. I came to the land where that man had died, and I learned that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had said this about him. I found him lying outside his grave. I inquired: ""What is the matter with him?"" The people said: ""We buried him, but the earth did not accept him."
"745","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Previously, a book would be revealed from one door according to one letter, but the Qur’an has been revealed from seven doors according to seven letters (they are): ‘Warner, Commanding, Lawful, Unlawful, Definitive, Allegorical, and Parables.’ So you should declare its lawful as lawful, its unlawful as unlawful, act upon what you have been commanded in it, and refrain from what you have been forbidden from. Take lesson from its parables, act upon its commands, have faith in its allegorical verses, and say: ‘We believe in it. All of it is from our Lord.’”"
"746","I heard a man reciting a verse; the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had taught me to recite that verse, but that man was reciting it in a different manner. I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was whispering something to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). I mentioned this matter to him, so Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) turned towards us and said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah has commanded you people to recite in the manner in which you have been taught."
"747","I came to the mosque in the evening, and some people came and sat near me. I said to one of them: Recite (the Qur'an) before me. So he recited some words in a manner that I had not learned. I asked: Who taught you this recitation? He replied: The Messenger of Allah taught me this recitation. Then we set out and presented ourselves before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). I said: We have differed regarding the recitation. Upon hearing this, the blessed face of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) changed, and when I mentioned the difference, he was greatly saddened by it. He said: The people before you were destroyed because of their differences. Then he instructed Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah commands you that each of you should recite in the manner in which he was taught, because the people before you were destroyed due to their differences. The narrator says: Then we left from there, and each of us would recite in the manner he had learned, and his companion would not recite in his manner."
"748","I did not fear that people would gather around me, I would have demonstrated this way of recitation."
"749","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Beautify the Qur'an with your voices."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) These are the words from which a contradictory meaning is sometimes taken. What is meant by the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is: You should beautify the Qur'an with your voices, not that you should beautify your voices with the Qur'an."
"750","The Prophet ﷺ said: Beautify the Qur'an with your voices. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1468)"
"751","God has not listened to anything as He listens to a Prophet reciting the Qur'an in a sweet voice. (Using translation from Muslim 792a)"
"752","Allah has not heard anything (more pleasing) than listening to the Prophet reciting the Qur'an in a sweet loud voice. (Using translation from Muslim 793b)"
"753","I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying and a sound came from his breast like the rumbling of a mill owing to weeping. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 904)"
"754","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Allah listens more attentively to a man with a beautiful voice who recites Qur’an out loud than the master of a singing slave listens to his slave.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1340)"
"755","The narrator named Basheer says: I asked Waleed: Who are these three people? He replied: The hypocrite is the one who denies the Qur'an, the wicked is the one who takes compensation for it, and the believer is the one who has faith in it."
"756","The narrator says: I submitted, O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to benefit from my strength and youth. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Recite the entire Qur'an in twenty days. I submitted, O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to benefit from my strength and youth. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Recite it in ten days. I submitted, O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to benefit from my strength and youth. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Recite it in seven days. I submitted, O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to benefit from my strength and youth, but the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not accept this from me."
"757","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Recite it in ten days. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to benefit from my strength and my youth. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Recite it in seven days. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to benefit from my strength and my youth. The narrator states: But the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not accept this from me."
"758","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Whoever recites (i.e., the entire Qur'an) in less than three days has not understood it. (Or, that person does not possess understanding and comprehension).\"""""
"759","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Continue reciting the Qur’an as long as your hearts are incli"
"760","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day came out to us while we were reciting the Qur’an. He said: Praise be to Allah. The Book of Allah is one, and among you are the red, and among you are the white and among you are the black. Recite it before there appear people who will recite it and straighten it as an arrow is straightened. They will get their reward for it in this world and will not get it in the Hereafter. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 831)"
"761","I have forgotten such-and-such verse. He does not forget it, rather that verse is made to be forgotten by him."
"762","I have forgotten such-and-such verse.’ He has not forgotten it, rather it has been made to be forgotten by him.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sa‘id did not narrate any other hadith as a “Musnad” narration from A‘mash except this narration."
"763","The Prophet ﷺ said: ""It is not right for any one of you to say: 'I have forgotten such and such a verse.' Rather, he has been caused to forget. Study the Qur'an, for it escapes from the heart of man faster than a camel escapes from its fetter. "" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 943)"
"764","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The example of the person who knows the Qur'an by heart is like the owner of tied camels. If he keeps them tied, he will control them, but if he releases them, they will run away."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5031)"
"765","""The likeness of the Quran is that of a hobbled camel. If its owner ties its rope, he will keep it, but if he loosens its rope it will go away."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3783)"
"766","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: One who was devoted to the Qur'an will be told to recite, ascend and recite carefully as he recited carefully when he was in the world, for he will reach his abode when he comes to the last verse he recites. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1464)"
"767","One who is skilled in the Qur'an is associated with the noble, upright recording angels, and he who falters when he recites the Qur'an and finds it difficult for him will have a double reward. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1454)"
"768","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a group of people sit in the mosque of Allah, reciting the Book of Allah and teaching it to one another, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, the angels surround them, and Allah mentions them to those who are with Him (the angels). And whoever is slowed down by his deeds, his lineage will not speed him up."
"769","The animal began to jump. The man saw a cloud that had covered him. That man went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned this matter to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O so-and-so! Continue reciting, that was tranquility which was descending because of the Qur’an (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) because of the Qur’an.”"
"770","The Prophet said: ""The likeness of the believer who recites the Qur'an is that of a citron, the taste and smell of which are good. The likeness of a believer who does not read the Qur'an is that of a date, the taste of which is good but it has no smell. The likeness of a hypocrite who reads the Qur'an is that of a sweet basil, the smell of which is good but its taste is bitter. And the likeness of a hypocrite who does not read the Qur'an is that of a colocynth (bitter apple), the taste of which is bitter and it has no smell.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 214)"
"771","""The Prophet [SAW] said: 'The parable of the believer who recites the Qur'an is that of a citron, the taste and smell of which are good. The parable of a believer who does not read the Qur'an is that of a date, the taste of which is good but it has no smell. The parable of a hypocrite who reads the Qur'an is that of basil, the smell of which is good but its taste is bitter. And the parable of a hypocrite who does not read the Qur'an is that of a colocynth (bitter-apple), the taste of which is bitter and it has no smell.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5038)"
"772","Whom have you appointed as your deputy over the people of the valley? He said: I have appointed Ibn Abza over them, ‘Umar said: Who is Ibn Abza? Nafiʼ said: One of our freed slaves. ‘Umar said: Have you appointed a freed slave over them? Nafi’ said: He has great knowledge of the Book of Allah, is well versed in the rules of inheritance (al­-fara'id) and is a (good) qadi (judge). 'Umar said. Indeed your Prophet ﷺ said, “Allah raises some people (in status) by means of this Book and brings others low by means of it.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 232)"
"773","I have grown old, my tongue has become heavy, and my heart has become hard (meaning my memory is weak). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then learn the three Surahs that begin with ""Ha Meem."" The man said similar words. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Teach me a comprehensive Surah. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) taught him Surah Az-Zalzalah, until when you reached this verse: ""So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it."" The man said: By the One Who has sent you with the truth, I will not care to learn anything more than this until I present myself before Allah, the Exalted. Tell me which deeds are obligatory upon me, I will do those deeds which I am able to do. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Perform the five prayers, fast in Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House of Allah, pay the Zakat from your wealth, enjoin good and forbid evil."
"774","I not tell you about the most excellent part of the Qur'an?"" The narrator states: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited before him: ""Alhamdulillahi Rabbil 'Alamin."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Shall I not tell you about the most excellent part of the Qur'an,"" means: (its recitation) is best for you. It does not mean that one part of the Qur'an is superior to another, because it is impossible for there to be preference (tafadul) in the speech of Allah Almighty (i.e., for one part to be given superiority over another)."
"775","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, did not reveal in the Tawrah or the Injil anything like Umm Al-Quran (Al-Fatihah), which is the seven oft-recited, and (Allah said) it is divided between Myself and My slave will have what he asked for.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 914)"
"776","I am behind the Imam, so Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) struck my arm and said: O Persian! Recite it in your heart, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this: ""Allah Almighty says: I have divided the prayer (i.e., the recitation of Surah Al-Fatihah) between Myself and My servant into two parts, half of it is for My servant and half is for Me, and My servant will have what he asks for. When the servant recites « » , Allah Almighty says: My servant has praised Me. When the servant recites 'Ar-Rahman Ar-Raheem', Allah Almighty says: My servant has extolled Me. When the servant recites « » , Allah Almighty says: My servant has glorified Me, and this (the following verse) is between Me and My servant, he says: ' « » ', and the remaining part after this is for My servant, and My servant will have what he asks for. He recites: 'Guide us to the straight path, the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who have evoked [Your] anger or of those who are astray.' (Allah Almighty says), so this thing will be given to My servant and My servant will have what he asks for."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Mughira is Abdul Quddus bin Hajjaj Khawlani."
"777","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed bin Mualla (may Allah be pleased with him) is Rafi‘ bin Mualla bin Lawdhan bin Haritha. He passed away in the year 74 Hijri."
"778","narrates: ""Once, Gabriel was sitting with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). During this, he heard the sound of a door opening above (in the sky). He raised his head and said: Today, such a door of the sky has opened which has never opened before. Then an angel came to them and said to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): Accept the glad tidings of two such Surahs which have not been given to any prophet before you; they are Surah Al-Fatihah and the last verses of Surah Al-Baqarah. Whatever letter of them you recite, you will be granted that thing."
"779","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""O Abu Usayd! Continue reciting."" I paid attention and saw some lights that were present between the sky and the earth. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""O Abu ‘Atiq! You are reciting."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Now I cannot continue reciting."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""These were angels who descended because of the recitation of Surah Al-Baqarah. If you had continued reciting, you would have seen even more astonishing things."
"780","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Everything has a pinnacle, and the pinnacle of the Qur’an is Surah Al-Baqarah. Whoever recites it at night, Satan will not enter his house for three nights, and whoever recites it during the day, Satan will not enter his house for three days.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), “Satan does not enter that house for three days,” refers to the rebellious devils. Other devils are not meant here."
"781","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him). I asked him about this matter, so he told me that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah Al-Baqarah at night, these two will suffice for him."
